35,2,1,talk,May,,The tally shows two people used it eleven times. The rest of us only four. It’s not shared.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The wall is one sheet of plasterboard. I could hear a phone call clearly. It’s useless for privacy.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,Eleven callouts last year for equipment. The store room had zero. We are paying for maintenance we don’t need.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"The quotes are high. 141,000 for a meeting setup, 96,000 for a kitchen. That’s a lot of yen.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The last awkward talk happened across the desks. Everyone heard it. We need a place where that doesn’t happen.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, if the wall is that thin, a quiet room is impossible unless we soundproof it.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, exactly. And the crumbs under the keyboards are getting worse. People are eating at their desks.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Sakura, the invoices show we paid 68,000 for outside hire. We are already spending money on this.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Servas, that confirms it. We are paying out monthly. We need to stop the leak.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@May, the round trip for lunch is twenty-five minutes. That’s why people eat at their desks.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"If we make it a kitchen, we solve the lunch problem. But who cleans the crumbs?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"A kitchen means more mess. I hate crumbs. A quiet room is better, but the wall is the issue.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,"A meeting space requires a screen and table. That’s the 141,000 quote. Is it worth it?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"The kitchen quote is cheaper, but the maintenance will be higher. We need to think about the long term.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"A meeting space could be bookable. That way, we don’t have to argue over who is in there.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,I like the idea of booking. It stops the first-come-first-served chaos.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"If it’s bookable, I can use it for quiet work. But I need to know if the noise is controlled.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,A bookable space is fair. It distributes the use. I am leaning towards that.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"If we book it, we can track the usage. That helps with the invoices and accountability.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,A meeting space feels right. It gives us a place to talk without the whole office listening.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
